            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner, the case concerns whether the OCC\u2019s Regulation\u202f7.40006 preempts Michigan state law that historically regulated the non\u2011bank, state\u2011chartered operating subsidiaries of national banks."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "4f1bb12224c2f72f9255b6072166f3f4a0e5ea8fd26a96cfd1a39e4fe913eea4",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-4f1bb12224c2-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioner argues that the dual banking system of state and federal regulation is a long\u2011standing example of cooperative federalism and that the OCC\u2019s rule disrupts the balance by depriving states of authority they have exercised for decades."
      }
    ],
